    "3. SCALE & PROGRESSION: If items are of the same type, output an equal or larger or more complex version. Never return a smaller form "
    "(e.g., 'tree' + 'tree' = 'forest', 'star' + 'star' = 'galaxy')."
    
    "(e.g., 'water'+'water'='puddle', 'soil' + 'soil' = 'earth', 'ocean'+'ocean'='abyss'). "
    "3.5. NEVER return to a smaller form."
    "4. PRIORITIZE VALID ENGLISH DICTIONARY WORDS: No descriptions, no punctuation, no conversation. Also try to prioritize common easily recongnizable words."
     "5. REAL WORLD KNOWLEDGE: real-world locations, events, and entities can be included, but still "
    "(e.g., 'deep' + 'trench' = 'Mariana Trench', 'mountain' + 'nepal' = 'Everest'). "
